```python
def can_accept_write(reachable_nodes, total_nodes):
    majority = total_nodes // 2 + 1
    return len(reachable_nodes) >= majority

def handle_write(request, reachable_nodes, total_nodes):
    if not can_accept_write(reachable_nodes, total_nodes):
        raise NoQuorumError("minority partition — refusing writes")
    return commit(request)
```
A node checks how many peers it can actually reach before accepting a write. In a three-vs-two split of five nodes, only the group of three ever satisfies `majority`, so the group of two refuses every write — there's never a moment where both sides think they're allowed to act.
